      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T20:13:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The uplink port is hardcoded as `ae0` here and in BASE_CONFIG_DELETE_COMMANDS (lines 88-91). On a switch whose uplink is named differently (ae1, a LAG LAG name, a 100G member), `set class-of-service interfaces ae0 ...` is accepted for a non-existent interface and the commit succeeds, so the base config installs cleanly but does nothing for real traffic. has_base_config() only greps STORAGE-CLASSIFIER, so it cannot catch that either. A parameter (or plugin config key) for the uplink would make this explicit.",
      "revId": "d1c33de6b67e648f34a55e5316faa7ee8f7f8106",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa7b91c4_0242c0a7",
        "filename": "src/quads/tools/external/juniper_roce.py",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 106,
