        "id": 1039965
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T20:13:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two states collapsed into one bool: if `SSHHelper` raises (auth failure, unreachable switch) or `run_cmd` returns False, this returns False, the same as \"config absent\". `configure()` then tells the operator to run `--install-roce` for what is really a login problem, and `uninstall_roce()` skips the switch as if it had no base config. Suggest returning None (or raising) when the check could not be performed, and handling that case separately in roce.py:173 and roce.py:121.",
      "revId": "d1c33de6b67e648f34a55e5316faa7ee8f7f8106",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bbb9bbd7_acaa6cda",
        "filename": "src/quads/tools/external/juniper_roce.py",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039965
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T20:13:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`Config.plugins[\"juniper\"][\"username\"]` raises KeyError when the juniper plugin is absent from plugins.yml, and only SSHHelperException is caught here. The KeyError escapes into roce.py:83 (install_roce calls has_base_config() outside its try) and aborts the rest of the switch list with a traceback, contrary to the documented log-and-continue behaviour. Resolve the username once in `__init__` and raise JuniperRoCEException with a clear message.",
      "revId": "d1c33de6b67e648f34a55e5316faa7ee8f7f8106",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
