      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T20:13:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`execute()` treats a prompt timeout as the only failure. Junos answers a bad `set`/`delete` (syntax error, unknown object) with an error message and a fresh prompt, so the loop keeps going and `commit` commits whatever survived, then `apply_base_config()` returns True. Checking `self.child.before` for \"syntax error\" / \"statement not found\" and raising JuniperRoCEException would make a partial commit impossible to miss.",
      "revId": "d1c33de6b67e648f34a55e5316faa7ee8f7f8106",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
